    "continue_owner": "The six Continue UI functions share their ContinueWork layout, two lifecycle descriptors, read-only two-coordinate cursor table and name, plus the EU-only language tile index. The surrounding msg prefix owns all six existing private text-state variables; the event/message suffix owns its sole scanline-scroll COMMON pointer. Sequential ordinary text and BSS links reproduce all original regional function addresses, bytes and RAM instances. This supports the bounded msg.c / continue_ui.c / event_message.c source organization; it does not claim every remaining event/message name and external asset provider has a recovered original boundary. Four shared prefix APIs now have declarations matching their definitions, replacing two incompatible Jiminy declarations."
